# Native SDK telemetry policy

Status: NOT_STARTED
Milestone: Explicit local-first network/privacy boundary
Dependencies: 03_BODY_FACE_TRACKING.todo

## Purpose
Resolve the prebuilt MediaPipe SDK's usage telemetry without confusing local inference with
network silence or suppressing warning text as if that disabled uploads.

## Tasks
- [x] Record native Clearcut upload warnings observed during the first recorded-video test.
- [x] Verify the upstream maintainer's explanation and absence of an official opt-out.
- [ ] Obtain direction on the acceptable SDK/network policy before making changes.
- [ ] Evaluate a source-built no-telemetry SDK or an explicitly authorized scoped network policy.
- [ ] Verify the chosen approach using synthetic/public inputs, not private user media.
- [ ] Requalify tracking/rendering and update documentation after any actual dependency change.

## Acceptance criteria
- [ ] The chosen network behavior is explicit, verified and accurately documented.
- [ ] No broad machine firewall/proxy changes, log-only suppression or input-data upload.

## Completion evidence
- Runtime emitted portable_clearcut_uploader.cc failures in normal playback and the
  exhaustive diagnostic pass. Those messages do not establish what packets were transmitted.
- Upstream issue: https://github.com/google-ai-edge/mediapipe/issues/6291
- Maintainer statement:
  https://github.com/google-ai-edge/mediapipe/issues/6291#issuecomment-4896121772
- The maintainer states telemetry is intentional, has no official opt-out, and never sends
  input data. They identify source builds or blocking the host as alternatives.
- Input exclusion is an upstream assertion, not independently verified packet contents.
- No SDK, firewall, proxy or application change was made during the first test.
- The earlier WINHTTP.dll startup failure is not proven to be caused by telemetry.

## Completion log
- 2026-10-12 - Discovered and documented; remediation awaits direction.
